From: bot-for-go[bot] <199222863+bot-for-go[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:51:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Default to PIE on Linux

Use PIE by default on Linux architectures that support internal PIE linking,
without requiring cgo or an external linker. Preserve the existing exe
default for other Linux targets and race-enabled builds, and keep explicit
-buildmode=exe as an opt-out.

Fixes microsoft/go#2236.
---
 src/internal/platform/supported.go | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/internal/platform/supported.go b/src/internal/platform/supported.go
index e54c1ac580cce130bd08043d6f90bfacd94721a7..19b3870814c385f34d3b4df5bf6f8ce8cdae668d 100644
--- a/src/internal/platform/supported.go
+++ b/src/internal/platform/supported.go
@@ -242,12 +242,15 @@ func InternalLinkPIESupported(goos, goarch string) bool {
 }
 
 // DefaultPIE reports whether goos/goarch produces a PIE binary when using the
-// "default" buildmode. On Windows this is affected by -race,
+// "default" buildmode. On some platforms this is affected by -race,
 // so force the caller to pass that in to centralize that choice.
 func DefaultPIE(goos, goarch string, isRace bool) bool {
 	switch goos {
 	case "android", "ios":
 		return true
+	case "linux":
+		// Preserve race support and builds without an external linker.
+		return !isRace && InternalLinkPIESupported(goos, goarch)
 	case "windows":
 		if isRace {
 			// PIE is not supported with -race on windows;
